From b8387ead07d08a440c5592b0781028044d2815a3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: a1go3 <116062404+a1go3@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 18:13:40 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] feat(reality): log a ClientHello nobody answers and report it
 as a stall

A provider filter that freezes a server address and port lets the TCP connection up and then drops the ClientHello, so the client only saw a timeout. A REALITY handshake that runs out of time now logs the server address and returns a HandshakeStallError, which VLESS dials keep wrapped up to URLTest. XHTTP transports dial apart from the stream, so their handshakes get the TLS timeout instead of waiting for good, and a dial that runs out of time while one still waits is reported as a stall.
